Z||000000||Tigger||08-07-2001||10:27 AM||||Well, I got back late last night from a weekend vacation/family reunion in Toronto.  I would have tried to make plans to maybe meet up with some from the forum, but I didn't have my Fiero and knew I wouldn't have much time to stop.  I'm going to try to make the GTA show next month.<P>Anyway, I kept my eyes peeled for Fieros on the road, here's what I saw.<P>Didn't see any Fieros on the trip over.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Relatives we stayed with are original owners of a nice white '84 SE.<P>Found out at the reunion that another relative worked on the dies and processes for making the bumpers for the Fiero.<P>Saw a real nice silver fastback parked at the Pickering Town Centre.<P>Seen a red 2m4 parked in a driveway also in Pickering.<P>On the way home, saw a black coupe or SE going east on the 401 just west of the 401/407 interchange.<P>Was that you eh?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||2
